atimes.com/india/evening-newswrap-trump-xi-and-putin-unveil-landmark-peace-declaration-govt-tweaks-validity-for-puc-certificates-and-more/articleshow/135989700.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-newswrap-trump-xi-and-putin-unveil-landmark-peace-declaration-govt-tweaks-validity-for-puc-certificates-and-more/articleshow/135989700.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T17:56:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135991365,imgsize-73174.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Next door, worlds apart: India's child malnutrition puzzle]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/next-door-worlds-apart-indias-child-malnutrition-puzzle/articleshow/135986199.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135986199.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Child malnutrition is shaped by several factors, including maternal education and household wealth. While India's stunting rate has declined nationally, problems such as child wasting persist. A closer look at the latest survey data reveals striking differences even between neighbouring districts and raises questions about what lies behind these gaps.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/next-door-worlds-apart-indias-child-malnutrition-puzzle/articleshow/135986199.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/next-door-worlds-apart-indias-child-malnutrition-puzzle/articleshow/135986199.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T17:43:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Arghya Prasun Roychowdhury</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135987066,imgsize-327206.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Hyderabadi biryani not preferred': Azam Khan takes veiled dig at Owaisi ahead of UP polls]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/hyderabadi-biryani-not-preferred-azam-khan-takes-veiled-dig-at-owaisi-ahead-of-up-polls/articleshow/135990408.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135990408.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/hyderabadi-biryani-not-preferred-azam-khan-takes-veiled-dig-at-owaisi-ahead-of-up-polls/articleshow/135990408.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/hyderabadi-biryani-not-preferred-azam-khan-takes-veiled-dig-at-owaisi-ahead-of-up-polls/articleshow/135990408.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T17:33:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135990572,imgsize-1189584.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘TN becoming Vice City’: Stalin targets Vijay over Rs 140-crore heroin haul in Chennai]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/tn-becoming-vice-city-stalin-targets-vijay-over-rs-140-crore-heroin-haul-in-chennai/articleshow/135988359.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135988359.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/tn-becoming-vice-city-stalin-targets-vijay-over-rs-140-crore-heroin-haul-in-chennai/articleshow/135988359.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/tn-becoming-vice-city-stalin-targets-vijay-over-rs-140-crore-heroin-haul-in-chennai/articleshow/135988359.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T16:44:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aadrita Halder</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135988602,imgsize-1905050.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India, Italy target €20bn trade by 2029, explore economic corridor linking Asia and Europe]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-italy-target-20bn-trade-by-2029-explore-economic-corridor-linking-asia-and-europe/articleshow/135988322.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135988322.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[India and Italy aim to elevate their bilateral trade to €20 billion by 2029, establishing dedicated task forces in both nations to help local businesses tackle bureaucratic hurdles more effectively. Furthermore, they explored the India-Middle East-Europe Economic Corridor, recognizing Italy's strategic ports like Trieste as crucial to boost trade connectivity. An exciting proposal also emerged for an Innovation Hub in India to strengthen technological collaborations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-italy-target-20bn-trade-by-2029-explore-economic-corridor-linking-asia-and-europe/articleshow/135988322.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-italy-target-20bn-trade-by-2029-explore-economic-corridor-linking-asia-and-europe/articleshow/135988322.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T16:39:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135988398,imgsize-94944.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[As Sonia Gandhi’s memoir draws attention, Sikh family preserves her ancestral home in Italian village]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/as-sonia-gandhis-memoir-draws-attention-sikh-family-preserves-her-ancestral-home-in-italian-village/articleshow/135986304.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135986304.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sukhdev Singh Kang has purchased the ancestral home of Sonia Gandhi located in Italy and intends to open a museum. The property, identified as Sonia Gandhi's birthplace, has garnered significant interest from Indian visitors. Kang's family aims to preserve her family's history through artifacts and personal items displayed at the museum. They also plan to meet with Sonia Gandhi and her children to enrich the museum experience.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/as-sonia-gandhis-memoir-draws-attention-sikh-family-preserves-her-ancestral-home-in-italian-village/articleshow/135986304.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/as-sonia-gandhis-memoir-draws-attention-sikh-family-preserves-her-ancestral-home-in-italian-village/articleshow/135986304.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T16:33:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yudhvir Rana</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135987579,imgsize-176132.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Saddened by the news': Stalin mourns VS Babu, who unseated him in Kolathur]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/saddened-by-the-news-stalin-mourns-vs-babu-who-unseated-him-in-kolathur/articleshow/135987719.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135987719.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/saddened-by-the-news-stalin-mourns-vs-babu-who-unseated-him-in-kolathur/articleshow/135987719.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/saddened-by-the-news-stalin-mourns-vs-babu-who-unseated-him-in-kolathur/articleshow/135987719.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T16:29:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135987904,imgsize-1576304.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[PUC rules changed: BS-I to BS-VI vehicles get new certificate validity periods; check yours]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/puc-rules-changed-bs-i-to-bs-vi-vehicles-get-new-certificate-validity-periods-check-yours/articleshow/135985582.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135985582.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The ministry of road transport and highways recently unveiled revised regulations concerning pollution under control certificates. The new guidelines offer longer validity for BS-VI vehicles based on their age and usage while mandating more frequent emission checks for older vehicles. Furthermore, there will be a standardised validity period for older emission categories throughout India, enhancing compliance and promoting uniformity in emission standards.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/puc-rules-changed-bs-i-to-bs-vi-vehicles-get-new-certificate-validity-periods-check-yours/articleshow/135985582.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/puc-rules-changed-bs-i-to-bs-vi-vehicles-get-new-certificate-validity-periods-check-yours/articleshow/135985582.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-19T15:34:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135985913,imgsize-70588.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Delhi HC clarifies restaurants have no interim relief to levy mandatory service charges]]></title><description><![CDATA[]]></description><